a steady stream of people signing the  book of condolences in henley on thames  the people who live in this  quintessentially english town would hold  the queen and the royal family close to  their hearts  the regular mid-afternoon mass took on a  different feel in many ways this became  one of the first memorial services to  queen elizabeth ii  the news of the queen's passing  genuinely seems to have come as quite a  shock to many here  it's something the clergy had  anticipated and believed that in the  coming days they will be called upon to  give support and guidance  i think that people will probably be  almost slightly taken by surprise it's a  thing that i often say when people live  very long that although you feel that it  shouldn't be a shock  and that everybody would have expected  it actually the fact that they've lived  so long you start to feel almost like  that the person is kind of eternal like  like the kind of rocks under our  feet and in a way it actually makes it  more difficult and so i think that  people will be taken by surprise  henley is a sleepy place for sure but  there was something different a sort of  sense of loss people not quite sure what  to do with themselves  we heard that she was resting which we'd  heard before and um  one presumed uh eventually she'd be all  right and then you suddenly heard she  died and  was quite shocked  the length and breadth of the uk people  have their own memories and their own  stories about the queen i had the  privilege to work  for her majesty with angela kelly on a  book  for the diamond jubilee  bernard connolly collaborated on a book  celebrating the queen's coronation he  ended up working for her for three years  like so many others she changed his life  she was very  humble  and very kind  and just  a very patient woman actually i found  and a  naughty sense of humor  [Music]  the queen has passed and we now have a  king and that is how it works a  centuries-old tradition that ensures we  always have a figurehead  it means that nothing has changed  although of course in reality everything  has changed  mr ramsey sky news henley on thames  [Music]
 

